  "id": "methadone",
  "term": "methadone",
  "definition": "Methadone is a synthetic opioid drug that acts on central nervous system opioid receptors, especially the mu receptor, and has morphine-like effects such as pain relief, sedation, euphoria, and physical dependence. Compared with other morphine-like opioids, its withdrawal tends to begin more slowly, last longer, and be less severe.",
